  "summary": "This paper proposes a QFT-based quantum integer comparator using one ancilla qubit and 2n^2 CR gates, then extends it to modular reduction and modular addition with 8 QFT(IQFT) operations and 5n^2 CR-gate operations. It further derives modular multiplication and exponentiation constructions requiring 2n + 1 and 3n + 1 qubits, respectively, with O(n^3) depth and O(n^3 log n) size, but reports no hardware experiments or classical benchmark comparisons.",
